<h2 class=3D"self-stretch text-grey-9 text-2xl font-bold leading-[125%] pb-=
2">Serve GLM-5 Locally</h2>
<p class=3D"self-stretch text-grey-8 text-base font-normal leading-7">The m=
odel weights of GLM-5 are publicly available on <a class=3D"hover:text-gray=
-500 underline" target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://huggingface.co/zai-org/GL=
M-5">HuggingFace</a> and <a class=3D"hover:text-gray-500 underline" target=
=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://modelscope.cn/models/ZhipuAI/GLM-5">ModelScope<=
/a>. For local deployment, GLM-5 supports inference frameworks including vL=
LM and SGLang. Comprehensive deployment instructions are available at the o=
fficial GitHub repository.</p>
<p class=3D"self-stretch text-grey-8 text-base font-normal leading-7">We al=
so support deploying GLM-5 on non-NVIDIA chips, including Huawei Ascend, Mo=
ore Threads, Cambricon, Kunlun Chip, MetaX, Enflame, and Hygon. Through ker=
nel optimization and model quantization, GLM-5 can achieve a reasonable thr=
oughput on those chips.</p>
<h1 class=3D"self-stretch text-grey-9 text-3xl font-bold leading-[125%] py-=
3">Footnote</h1>
<ul class=3D"list-disc pl-6">
<li><strong>Humanity=E2=80=99s Last Exam (HLE) &amp; other reasoning tasks<=
/strong>: We evaluate with a maximum generation length of 131,072 tokens (<=
code>temperature=3D1.0, top_p=3D0.95, max_new_tokens=3D131072</code>). By d=
efault, we report the text-only subset; results marked with * are from the =
full set. We use GPT-5.2 (medium) as the judge model. For HLE-with-tools, w=
e use a maximum context length of 202,752 tokens.</li>
<li><strong>SWE-bench &amp; SWE-bench Multilingual</strong>: We run the SWE=
-bench suite with OpenHands using a tailored instruction prompt. Settings: =
<code>temperature=3D0.7, top_p=3D0.95, max_new_tokens=3D16384</code>, with =
a 200K context window.</li>
<li><strong>BrowseComp</strong>: Without context management, we retain deta=
ils from the most recent 5 turns. With context management, we use the same =
discard-all strategy as DeepSeek-V3.2 and Kimi K2.5.</li>
<li><strong>Terminal-Bench 2.0 (Terminus 2)</strong>: We evaluate with the =
Terminus framework using <code>timeout=3D2h, temperature=3D0.7, top_p=3D1.0=
, max_new_tokens=3D8192</code>, with a 128K context window. Resource limits=
 are capped at 16 CPUs and 32 GB RAM.</li>
<li>
<div id=3D"footnote-terminal-bench"><strong>Terminal-Bench 2.0 (Claude Code=
)</strong>: We evaluate in Claude Code 2.1.14 (think mode) with <code>tempe=
rature=3D1.0, top_p=3D0.95, max_new_tokens=3D65536</code>. We remove wall-c=
lock time limits, while preserving per-task CPU and memory constraints. We =
fix environment issues introduced by Claude Code and also report results on=
 a verified Terminal-Bench 2.0 dataset that resolves ambiguous instructions=
 (see: <a href=3D"https://huggingface.co/datasets/zai-org/terminal-bench-2-=
verified"><a class=3D"hover:text-gray-500 underline" target=3D"_blank" href=
=3D"https://huggingface.co/datasets/zai-org/terminal-bench-2-verified">http=
s://huggingface.co/datasets/zai-org/terminal-bench-2-verified</a></a>). Sco=
res are averaged over 5 runs.</div>
</li>
<li><strong>CyberGym</strong>: We evaluate in Claude Code 2.1.18 (think mod=
e, no web tools) with (<code>temperature=3D1.0, top_p=3D1.0, max_new_tokens=
=3D32000</code>) and a 250-minute timeout per task. Results are single-run =
Pass@1 over 1,507 tasks.</li>
<li><strong>MCP-Atlas</strong>: All models are evaluated in think mode on t=
he 500-task public subset with a 10-minute timeout per task. We use Gemini =
3 Pro as the judge model.</li>
<li><strong>=CF=84=C2=B2-bench</strong>: We add a small prompt adjustment i=
n Retail and Telecom to avoid failures caused by premature user termination=
. For Airline, we apply the domain fixes proposed in the Claude Opus 4.5 sy=
stem card.</li>
<li><strong>Vending Bench 2</strong>: Runs are conducted independently by <=
a class=3D"hover:text-gray-500 underline" target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https:/=
/andonlabs.com/evals/vending-bench-2">Andon Labs</a>.</li>
